{"name":"Chianti","hex":"#734342","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Chianti","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hilly geographic region in central Tuscany, Italy, famous for red wines.","A Tuscan red wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Chianti"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chianti","blocks":[{"text":"Chianti is an Italian red wine produced in the Chianti region of central Tuscany, principally from the Sangiovese grape. It was historically associated with a squat bottle enclosed in a straw basket, called a fiasco. However, the fiasco is now only used by a few makers of the wine; most Chianti is bottled in more standard-shaped wine bottles. In the late 19th century, Baron Bettino Ricasoli helped establish Sangiovese as the blend's dominant grape variety, creating the blueprint for today's Chianti wines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Fiasco_di_vino_rosso_da_tavola_Monteriggioni.jpg/330px-Fiasco_di_vino_rosso_da_tavola_Monteriggioni.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chianti"},{"title":"Chianti (region)","blocks":[{"text":"Chianti, in Italy also referred to as Monti del Chianti or Colline del Chianti, is a mountainous area of Tuscany in the provinces of Florence, Siena and Arezzo, composed mainly of hills and mountains. It is known for the wine produced in and named for the region, Chianti."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sottozone_chianti_it.jpg/330px-Sottozone_chianti_it.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chianti_(region)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Grand_Duke_CosimoIII_of_Tuscany_by_van_Douven.jpg/250px-Grand_Duke_CosimoIII_of_Tuscany_by_van_Douven.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/88/Grand_Duke_CosimoIII_of_Tuscany_by_van_Douven.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Grand_Duke_CosimoIII_of_Tuscany_by_van_Douven.jpg/250px-Grand_Duke_CosimoIII_of_Tuscany_by_van_Douven.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In 1716 Cosimo III de' Medici, the Grand Duke of Tuscany, legislated the first official boundaries of the Chianti region in what is today part of the Chianti Classico DOCG.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrand_Duke_CosimoIII_of_Tuscany_by_van_Douven.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/Bettino_Ricasoli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/Bettino_Ricasoli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Baron Bettino Ricasoli developed the first \"modern\" Chianti recipe that was Sangiovese based.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABettino_Ricasoli.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Italian_DOCG_Chianti_label.jpg/500px-Italian_DOCG_Chianti_label.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Italian_DOCG_Chianti_label.jpg/1280px-Italian_DOCG_Chianti_label.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Italian_DOCG_Chianti_label.jpg/500px-Italian_DOCG_Chianti_label.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Italian DOCG Chianti label","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AItalian_DOCG_Chianti_label.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Sottozone_chianti.